                                                                  3034 1451
  Temperatures = 293.6 400 500 600 700 800 K                      3034 1451
                                                                  3034 1451
 HISTORY                                                          3034 1451
 -------                                                          3034 1451
 This evaluation was generated by Naval Nuclear Laboratory (Mar   3034 1451
 2023) [1] using the FLASSH code [2].  The physical model is      3034 1451
 based on the mixed elastic scattering treatment and includes     3034 1451
 coherent elastic scattering, incoherent elastic scattering and   3034 1451
 inelastic scattering contributions. This evaluation is intended  3034 1451
 to be used with the companion D(7LiD) TSL evaluation when        3034 1451
 modeling enriched 7LiD.                                          3034 1451
                                                                  3034 1451
 THEORY                                                           3034 1451
 ------                                                           3034 1451
 Lithium hydride (LiD) has a fluorite (NaCl) type face-centered   3034 1451
 cubic crystal structure with four Li and D atoms per unit call.  3034 1451
 The inelastic scattering cross sections were calculated in the   3034 1451
 incoherent approximation using the Li-7 partial phonon density   3034 1451
 of states from a VASP/PHONON calculation of 7LiD based on the    3034 1451
 crystal structure and lattice constant from [3].  The mixed      3034 1451
 elastic scattering treatment was used to account for both        3034 1451
 coherent and incoherent elastic scattering effects present in    3034 1451
 this material.  The coherent elastic scattering component was    3034 1451
 calculated in the cubic approxiation using the FLASSH            3034 1451
 generalized coherent elastic scattering module using the 7LiD    3034 1451
 crystal structure and measured room temperature lattice          3034 1451
 constant of 4.0684 Ang [3] along with free atom coherent         3034 1451
 scattering cross sections of 0.51 b for Li-7 from [5] and 2.483  3034 1451
 b for D from [4]. The incoherent elastic scattering component    3034 1451
 was calculated using the Debye-Waller factor derived from the    3034 1451
 Li-7 partial phonon density of states and a Li-7 free atom       3034 1451
 incoherent scattering cross section of 0.46 b from [5].  A Li-7  3034 1451
 free atom total scattering cross section of 0.97 b was used to   3034 1451
 ensure consistency with the ENDF/B-VIII.1 Li-7 evaluation. A     3034 1451
 phonon order of 500 was used to ensure both the inelastic        3034 1451
 scattering cross section and the S(alpha,beta) functions at      3034 1451
 elevated temperatures were adaquately converged.                 3034 1451
